PREPARED, NOT ADOPTED — READ THIS BLOCK BEFORE THE REPOSITORY IS MADE PUBLIC
============================================================================

This file was drafted by plan 08-03 to close the §17 structural requirement that
a repository carry a licence. Choosing a licence is a LEGAL DECLARATION about the
repository owner's own coursework, and no agent is entitled to make it. It is
therefore prepared, committed locally, and NOT published: nothing in this
repository has been pushed, no tag exists, and no remote has been touched.

MIT is the conventional academic default and is what is drafted below. Before
08-12 makes either repository public, the owner must explicitly confirm:

  1. that MIT is the licence they want (BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0 and "all rights
     reserved" are the usual alternatives, and a university may have a policy);
  2. that the copyright holder line names them correctly;
  3. that the year is right.

Registered as requiring that confirmation in `docs/SUBMISSION-CHECKLIST.md`
(row G6-03, open question OQ8-5) and in the publish runbook. Delete this block
once the owner has confirmed; the licence text below it is complete and standard.

